extends ../layout-marketing

block vars
	- metadata = {title: 'Help'}
	- isWebsiteRedesign = true

block content
	main#main-content.content
		.container
			.row
				.col-lg-8.offset-lg-2
					h1 Help
					p
						| #{settings.appName} is the Institute's collaborative LaTeX editor. This page covers the platform itself; for LaTeX, start with the guides below.

					h2.h3#first-project Start your first project
					ol
						li Log in with your IIT Mandi Google account.
						li Click <strong>New project</strong>, then <strong>Blank project</strong>. Give the project a name.
						li Type in the editor on the left. A LaTeX file is plain text; the commands in it start with a backslash, such as <code>\section{Introduction}</code>.
						li Click <strong>Recompile</strong>. The PDF appears on the right.
						li To start from a ready-made layout instead, see #[a(href='#templates') Start from a template].

					h2.h3#templates Start from a template
					ol
						li Click <strong>New project</strong>, then <strong>More templates</strong> and <strong>All templates</strong>, or open the #[a(href='/templates') template gallery].
						li
							| Pick the one that fits (see
							|
							a(href='#which-template') Which template to use
							| ).
						li Open the project and click <strong>Recompile</strong>. Replace the sample text with your own.
						li To change the font size, line spacing or margins, choose <strong>Format › Page setup</strong>. See #[a(href='#visual-editor') Editing without knowing LaTeX].
					h3.h4#which-template Which template to use
					ul
						li
							strong IIT Mandi Thesis
							|  — a PhD, MS (by Research), M.Tech (by Research) or I-PhD thesis.
						li
							strong IIT Mandi Project Report
							|  — a DP, ISTP, MTP, M.Tech or M.Sc project, by one student or a group.
						li
							strong IIT Mandi Lab Report
							|  — a report on a lab experiment.
						li
							strong IIT Mandi Assignment
							|  — numbered problems with marks, and your solutions.
						li
							strong IIT Mandi Presentation
							|  — slides for a talk, a seminar or a viva.
						li
							strong IIT Mandi Research Poster
							|  — an A0 portrait poster for a conference or a poster session.
						li
							strong IIT Mandi Formal Letter
							|  — a letter you write yourself, such as an application. It is not the Institute's official letterhead.
						li
							strong IIT Mandi Resume
							|  — a one-page resume for placements and internships.
					p
						| The thesis, project report and resume templates follow the best sources available, not an official circular. Check the current guidelines of the Academic Section or the Career and Placement Cell before you submit.

					h2.h3#faq Common questions
					details#faq-compile-paused
						summary Why did my compile pause?
						p
							if settings.compileQueue && settings.compileQueue.turnMs
								| When other people are waiting for a compile slot, a long compile pauses after #{Math.round(settings.compileQueue.turnMs / 1000)} seconds and lets the next one run. Yours carries on by itself when a slot is free. You don't need to click anything.
							else
								| When other people are waiting for a compile slot, a long compile pauses and lets the next one run. Yours carries on by itself when a slot is free. You don't need to click anything.
						p
							| If a compile reaches its time limit, the PDF shows the pages finished so far. See
							|
							a(href='#compile-time') Long documents and compile time
							| .
					if settings.editorPlaces && settings.editorPlaces.limit > 0
						details#faq-waiting-room
							summary Why am I in a waiting room?
							p
								| Only a limited number of people can have the editor open at once, so that editing stays fast. Keep the tab open. Your project opens by itself when a place is free. See
								|
								a(href='#editor-waiting-room') When the editor is full
								| .
					if settings.storageQuota && settings.storageQuota.defaultMB > 0
						details#faq-storage-full
							summary My storage is full. What can I do?
							ol
								li Open your account settings and look at the list of your largest projects.
								li Delete files you no longer need, or delete old projects and empty the trash.
								li If you still need more space, write to the address under Contact.
							p
								| See
								|
								a(href='#storage') Storage space
								| .
					details#faq-share-link
						summary Why does a share link open the project read-only?
						p
							if settings.shareLinksCanEdit === false
								| A share link only lets people view a project. To let someone edit, open
								|
								strong Share
								|
								| in the editor and invite them by their IIT Mandi email address as an editor.
							else
								| A link set to view-only lets people read the project but not change it. To let someone edit, open
								|
								strong Share
								|
								| in the editor and invite them by their IIT Mandi email address as an editor, or turn on the edit link.
					details#faq-restore-version
						summary How do I go back to an earlier version?
						ol
							li Open the project, then choose <strong>History</strong>.
							li Click a version in the list to see what the project looked like then.
							li To bring back one file, choose it on the left and click <strong>Restore this version</strong>.
							li To bring back the whole project, open the menu (⋮) next to the version and choose <strong>Restore project to this version</strong>.
					details#faq-tex-live-year
						summary Which TeX Live year should I choose?
						p
							| Each project compiles with one TeX Live release, and new projects use the newest. To change it, open the project, click <strong>Settings</strong>, open the <strong>Compiler</strong> tab, and choose a TeX Live version. Choose an older year only if a document written earlier fails to compile on the newest one. Packages differ between years, so changing the year can change the PDF. Compile again and check the result.
					details#faq-one-chapter
						summary How do I compile only one chapter?
						ol
							li Put each chapter in its own file and load it in the main file with <code>\include{chapter3}</code>. If the main file uses <code>\input{chapter3}</code>, change it to <code>\include</code>: only chapters loaded with <code>\include</code> can be skipped, and each one starts on a new page.
							li Compile the whole document once. This saves the page numbers and references of every chapter.
							li Add <code>\includeonly{chapter3}</code> to the preamble, the part of the main file before <code>\begin{document}</code>.
							li Compile again. Only that chapter is typeset. The line changes the PDF for everyone working on the project, so remove it when you want the whole document.
					details#faq-errors
						summary How do I read a compile error?
						ol
							li Open the logs next to the PDF.
							li Find the first error. Later errors often follow from it.
							li Read the line number it gives and look at that line in your file.
							if settings.askAi && settings.askAi.url
								li Click the sparkle button on the error to ask #{settings.askAi.name} what it means. See <a href="#ask-ai">Ask AI</a>.
							else
								li Search the message on <a href="https://tex.stackexchange.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TeX Stack Exchange</a>.
					details#faq-report-problem
						summary How do I report a problem?
						p
							| Write to
							|
							a(href='mailto:' + settings.adminEmail) #{settings.adminEmail}
							| . Include the address of the page, what you did, and what you expected. Copy the error text if there is one. There is no guaranteed reply time.

					h2.h3#visual-editor Editing without knowing LaTeX
					ul
						li
							| Choose
							|
							strong Visual
							|
							| above the editor to edit headings, lists, bold and italic text, tables and figures as they look, rather than as code. The PDF on the right follows when you recompile.
						li
							strong Format › Page setup
							|
							| (also the line-spacing button at the start of the toolbar) changes the font size, line spacing (single, 1.5 or double), margins, paper size and font of the whole document, and recompiles. It works in the main file, the one that starts with
							|
							code \documentclass
							| .
						li
							strong Insert › IIT Mandi logo
							|
							| puts the Institute logo where the cursor is. New blank projects already show it at the top; delete those lines if you don't need it.
						li
							| To find where something in the PDF comes from, double-click it in the PDF: the editor jumps to that place.
						li
							| Undo (Ctrl+Z) takes back the last changes, and
							|
							strong History
							|
							| restores any earlier version.

					h2.h3 Learning LaTeX
					ul
						li
							a(href='https://www.learnlatex.org/' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer') Learn LaTeX
							|  — short lessons for beginners, with examples to try.
						li
							a(href='https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/LaTeX' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer') LaTeX Wikibook
							|  — a reference for document structure, tables, figures, mathematics and bibliographies.
						li
							a(href='https://ctan.org/' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer') CTAN
							|  — the documentation of every LaTeX package.

					h2.h3 Fixing compile errors
					ul
						li
							| The logs next to the PDF list each error with the line that caused it. Fix the first error first: the ones after it often follow from it.
						li
							| For an unfamiliar message, search
							|
							a(href='https://tex.stackexchange.com/' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer') TeX Stack Exchange
							| .
						li
							| If the PDF stops updating or looks out of date, choose
							|
							strong Recompile from scratch
							|
							| in the Recompile menu.
						li
							| When many people compile at the same time, your compile waits for a free slot and starts on its own.

					h2.h3#compile-time Long documents and compile time
					ul
						li
							| Every compile has a time limit.
							if settings.compileQueue && settings.compileQueue.turnMs
								|
								| While others are waiting, a long compile pauses every #{Math.round(settings.compileQueue.turnMs / 1000)} seconds and carries on when a slot is free, so a thesis still compiles when the server is busy. Time spent paused does not count towards the limit.
						li
							| When a compile reaches its limit, or you stop it, the PDF shows the pages typeset up to that point. The next compile reuses the files it left behind, so it is usually faster.
						li
							| LaTeX typesets the whole document in every compile, but it does not have to draw every picture again. Load
							|
							code \usepackage{memoize}
							|
							| before TikZ or pgfplots: each picture is then drawn once and reused until you change it. In our test, a document with eight plots went from 78 seconds for the first compile to 3 seconds for the next ones. After you change a picture, it can appear once more on an extra page at the end of the PDF; the next compile removes it. The IIT Mandi thesis and project report templates already load memoize and compile again by themselves, so they never show that page.
						li
							| Pictures are saved only when a compile finishes. If a long document stops at its time limit, none of its new pictures are saved: compile part of it first (see the next tip), then the whole document. If a picture looks out of date, or after you change a setting that every picture uses (a font or a pgfplots style), choose
							|
							strong Recompile from scratch
							|
							| in the Recompile menu. It clears the saved pictures, and the next compile draws them all again.
						li
							| For a thesis, put each chapter in its own file and load it with
							|
							code \include{chapter3}
							| . While you work on one chapter, add
							|
							code \includeonly{chapter3}
							|
							| to the preamble: only that chapter is typeset, and its page numbers and references to other chapters stay correct.
						li
							| The
							|
							strong Fast [draft]
							|
							| compile mode in the Recompile menu leaves out images while you write.
						li
							| Large images slow every compile down: scale them to the size at which they are printed.

					h2.h3 Sharing and collaborating
					ul
						li
							| Use
							|
							strong Share
							|
							if settings.shareLinksCanEdit === false
								| in the editor to invite people by their IIT Mandi email address as viewers or editors, or to turn on a view-only link. Nobody can edit a project unless its owner invited them by name.
							else
								| in the editor to invite people by their IIT Mandi email address, or to turn on view-only and edit links.
						li
							| Shared projects and links open only after logging in with an IIT Mandi account.
						li
							strong History
							|
							| shows every change to a project and can restore earlier versions.

					h2.h3#review Comments and suggested changes
					p
						| Use these when a supervisor or a teammate reads your work: they can leave comments and suggest changes without overwriting your text.
					ul
						li
							| To comment, select some text in the editor and click
							|
							strong Add comment
							| . Comments show beside the text in the
							|
							strong Review
							|
							| panel, where anyone on the project can reply. Click the tick on a comment to mark it resolved; resolved comments stay under
							|
							strong Resolved comments
							| .
						li
							| To suggest changes instead of making them, click the pencil button in the editor toolbar, next to
							|
							strong Code
							|
							| and
							|
							strong Visual
							| , and choose
							|
							strong Reviewing
							| . What you type and delete is then shown as a suggestion, marked in colour, until someone accepts or rejects it.
						li
							| In the
							|
							strong Review
							|
							| panel, click the tick on a suggestion to accept it, or the cross to reject it.
						li
							| When you share a project, you can give someone the
							|
							strong Reviewer
							|
							| role. A reviewer can comment and suggest changes, but cannot change the text directly. Give it to a supervisor who should mark up a draft without editing it.

					h2.h3 Projects
					ul
						li
							| Archiving a project hides it from your project list without deleting it.
						if settings.retention && settings.retention.trashDays > 0
							li
								| Projects you own are deleted #{settings.retention.trashDays} days after you move them to the trash, so take back anything you still need before then.
						li
							| A project you delete from the trash cannot be restored by you. An administrator can recover it for #{Math.round(settings.projectHardDeletionDelay / 86400000)} days; after that it is removed for good.

					if settings.storageQuota && settings.storageQuota.defaultMB > 0
						h2.h3#storage Storage space
						ul
							li
								| Each account has #{settings.storageQuota.defaultMB} MB for the files and documents in the projects it owns, including archived projects and projects in the trash. Projects shared with you count towards their owner's space, not yours.
							if settings.storageQuota.maxMB > settings.storageQuota.defaultMB
								li
									| Those #{settings.storageQuota.defaultMB} MB are always yours, and you are not stopped there: while the server has room, you can use up to #{settings.storageQuota.maxMB} MB. If the server runs low on space, people using more than #{settings.storageQuota.defaultMB} MB are asked to free some before adding files.
							li
								| The project list and your account settings show how much you are using, and the settings list your largest projects. Earlier versions kept in a project's history don't count.
							li
								| To free space, delete files you no longer need, or delete old projects from the trash.
							li
								| If your work needs more space, for example a thesis with many images, write to
								|
								a(href='mailto:' + settings.adminEmail) #{settings.adminEmail}
								| .

					if settings.askAi && settings.askAi.url
						h2.h3#ask-ai Ask AI
						ul
							li
								strong Ask AI
								|
								| in the editor toolbar opens #{settings.askAi.name} in a window beside the editor, with the text you selected. The sparkle button on a compile error asks it what causes the error and how to fix it.
							li
								| #{settings.askAi.name} is an outside service, not part of #{settings.appName}. You use it with your own account, and what you send goes to its provider, so leave out anything confidential.
							li
								| To see both at once, move the editor window to the left half of your screen.

					if settings.editorPlaces && settings.editorPlaces.limit > 0
						h2.h3#editor-waiting-room When the editor is full
						ul
							li
								if settings.editorPlaces.maxLimit > settings.editorPlaces.limit
									| To keep editing fast for everyone, the number of people who can have the editor open at once depends on how busy the server is: at least #{settings.editorPlaces.limit}, and up to #{settings.editorPlaces.maxLimit} while it has room.
								else
									| To keep editing fast for everyone, at most #{settings.editorPlaces.limit} people can have the editor open at the same time.
							li
								| When it is full, opening a project shows your place in the queue. Keep that tab open: the project opens by itself as soon as a place is free.
							li
								| After #{settings.editorPlaces.idleMinutes} minutes without typing, clicking or scrolling, your place goes to the next person waiting. When you come back, you get a free place again, or a place in the queue.

					if settings.enableGitBridge
						h2.h3#git Git
						p
							| You can clone, pull and push projects with git, and work on them on your own computer.
						ol
							li
								| Open your
								|
								a(href='/user/settings') account settings
								| , find
								|
								strong Git integration
								|
								| and click
								|
								strong Generate token
								| . Copy the token and keep it safe: it is shown only once.
							li
								| Open the project, click
								|
								strong Integrations
								|
								| on the left edge of the editor, then
								|
								strong Git
								| . Copy the
								|
								code git clone
								|
								| command it shows and run it in a terminal.
							li
								| When git asks for a password, paste the token. Your Google password does not work here.
							li
								| Work as with any git repository. After
								|
								code git push
								| , the changes appear in the editor. Pull before you start, so that you have the changes made in the editor.
						p
							| If you can only view or review a project, you can pull from it but not push.

					h2.h3 Browsers
					p
						| Use a version of Chrome, Firefox, Safari or Edge released in the last year. Older browsers, and Internet Explorer, are not supported.

					h2.h3 Contact
					p
						| For questions, problems with your account or anything this page doesn't answer, write to
						|
						a(href='mailto:' + settings.adminEmail) #{settings.adminEmail}
						| .
